  "verbalization": "Br-Xanthone A is implicated in the interaction with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through a series of molecular targets. The evidence suggests that Br-Xanthone A acts as a target for WM-115, which in turn is a target of lactulose and Isobutyl hexanoate, all of which ultimately target UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. This indicates a potential pathway where Br-Xanthone A may influence the enzyme through its interaction with these intermediates. The scores from the three paths, which are consistent across different evidence sources, suggest a plausible and robust relationship between Br-Xanthone A and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. The mechanisms involve a chain of molecular interactions, where Br-Xanthone A serves as a starting point, leading through various compounds to the enzyme of interest. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
